course: dictionary
lesson: 10475
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tuna is a large, fast sea fish that lives in warm oceans. Tuna is also the meat of that fish, often sold in tins and used in sandwiches and salads. The same word can mean a living animal or food, so read the sentence to find out which.
explain: «Flying fish escape tuna and other hunters by leaping out and gliding on wing-like fins.» Here tuna are hunters that chase the flying fish, so tuna must mean the living fish. Try the swap check: put fish in place of tuna and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Now think about «a tin of tuna» on a shopping list. You cannot tin a living fish, so this tuna is the food. Words like tuna are nouns, and you can say a tuna, two tuna or tunas. When the context is not clear, check a dictionary.
fact: A tuna is a large, fast sea fish that lives in warm oceans.
fact: Tuna is also the meat of this fish, often sold in tins.
fact: Tuna are strong swimmers, and they are predators that eat smaller fish.
fact: «A tuna sandwich» and «tuna pasta» are common lunches, so tuna here means food.
fact: The context tells you the meaning: living animal in a science lesson, food in a lunchbox or shop.
exercise: What is a tuna? | A small brown bird | A fast car with a loud engine | A rock on the beach | *A large, fast sea fish that lives in warm oceans
exercise: A shopping list says «a tin of tuna». What does tuna mean here? | A kind of sea weed | A large, fast sea fish swimming in the ocean | *The meat of the fish, sold in tins | A pasta shape
exercise: «Flying fish escape tuna and other hunters.» Find and copy the word that names a large, fast sea fish. | hunters | *tuna | gliding | escape
test: «Tuna pasta is a common lunch.» What does tuna mean in this sentence? | A large, fast sea fish that swims in the ocean | *The food made from the fish meat | A school subject | A type of pasta shape
test: Ben buys three tins of tuna for a shopping sum. What are the tins holding? | Sea water | Bread | *Fish meat for eating | A rubbery toy
exam: Which sentence uses tuna to mean the living fish? | *«Tuna swim fast through warm oceans.» | «Tuna pasta is my favourite.» | «The tin of tuna was on sale.» | «I ate a tuna sandwich for lunch.»
